        "id": 8116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-05-21T15:36:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function must accept only parameters which are in the form returned by str2dn(), a list of list of 3-tuples, a somewhat obscure format. I\u0027m afraid someone seeing a function named is_dn_equal() might think they could pass strings as the 2 DN\u0027s. I suggest doing a isinstance(dn1, list) check before comparing the lengths and adding a :param: doc that clearly states the requirement. Note if someone does pass strings and the strings do not have equal length no exeception will be raised. Note, it\u0027s entirely possible for the 2 string representations to have unequal lengths but for the DN\u0027s compare as equal due to factors such as escaping, white space folding, etc.",
      "revId": "4ee9093b0431e4dcdc40bcd5f65475722dac3a95",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
